{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/2433-mummy-the-curse-video-review","id":2433,"title":"Mummy: The Curse - Video Review","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-03T23:28:32-08:00","id":2433,"title":"Mummy: The Curse - Video Review","content":"Herein for the viewing for you kindly folk is my long-in-the-making review of Mummy: The Curse - a game for which I've taken my time to grasp (or is reach?) the intricacies:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://youtu.be/ezqH26CjcAs\" data-code=\"ezqH26CjcAs\" data-provider=\"youtube_share\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/ezqH26CjcAs/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T07:34:19-08:00","id":2605,"title":"","content":"Very nice vid-review GG. Did you write that intro yourself? If so, could you post a transcript of it? Its very evocative and really helps to set the mood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:34:39-08:00","id":2688,"title":"","content":"Quite in depth. I agree with most of it but do have some things I found problematic that you didn't seem to find issues so I'd like to know how you found them.<br /> <br /> Mostly it's that the core book didn't give me much feel for what day to day life is actually like. Sure the first few hours get fiction pieces and it's relatively clear you're really confused and lost and barely look human but what about week 2 of your Descent? What do you get up to? How do you go about business? How do you contact your guilds and operate with them? Etc.<br /> <br /> I think that was the biggest thing I found lacking in the book. That and how guild could even function when only tiny fractions of the membership in a certain locale/nome would ever be active at the same time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/291-scutarii","name":"Scutarii","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"702"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T00:43:30-08:00","id":3256,"title":"","content":"JoeB: I did write the opening narrative myself, and once I'm home I'll post a transcript. Or rather, the full script. My recorded version is slightly abridged. Scutarii: You raise a very good point, but I find the motivation issue to be a similar case in most WoD games, and have largely taken it that most supernatural beings are individualistic to the point that they could pursue their own interests (combined of course in the case of Mummy, with that of their Judge). Regarding how Guilds contact one another, how they operate etc. I would agree that the core rulebook doesn't provide a huge amount of information on that subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T06:05:50-08:00","id":3412,"title":"","content":"Awesome, thanks GG!! I really found it very evocative and really sets the right mood for this game. I particularly loved the way you describe the feeling of an Arisen awakening to the senses of being alive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T11:30:27-08:00","id":3640,"title":"","content":"@JoeB<br /> <br /> <i>I awaken to darkness and the taste of perfume in my mouth. I try to lift an arm but find it fastened to my side. There is strength in that withered limb that would not seem possible, and with a concentrated flex my bonds are broken. My hand travels to my chin, my fingers probing the tattered skin and my cracked lips, before finally reaching the resins wedged inside my mouth. I pry them free and drop them to the ground, my jaw slowly closing for the first time in.. I\u2019m not sure how long.<br /> <br /> The taste of olibanum.. frankincense, remains. My eyes adjust to the darkness. Ah yes. Frankincense. A perfume with great meaning to me? But what? And why would I have locked it in my skull so as to be the first thing noticeable upon awakening? Hmm.<br /> <br /> Grinding my teeth despite their loose grip on my old gums, I wrench my other arm free and slide the lid off of my sarcophagus, feeling the tear of flesh from my back as some of it sticks to the surface while I move free. I feel the cold. I\u2019m not cold, but I feel the extreme in temperature. I step tentatively despite the Sekhem I feel coursing through my body. I know from the strength of my Ren, or name, that my Enlightened Senses will soon be capable of penetrating this pervasive black. No light at all in here. As I bump in to something hard that seems to swing gently from the ceiling with a metallic creak I focus. The taste of the perfume. The frankincense was there to help me remember something. Something important.<br /> <br /> I continue to push my way through this cool chamber, thick hanging articles, seemingly frozen to the touch being evaded as I go. My eyes have adjusted. My senses have penetrated this gloom. I am in a wide, tall and long rectangular tomb. The walls are bare, the hanging inventory is frozen meat. I have just pried myself free from some manner of cold box, clean and polished with small writing across the top that I cannot claim to understand in Iremite or indeed any other tongue I am aware of. Frigidaire.<br /> <br /> A momentary panic. I can feel the presence of vessels and relics surrounding me, the inventory decreed to me by the Judges for protection and use in times of need, but I cannot see them. That rage rises to the fore. That need to be free. With a strident walk, shoulders forward and eyes set, I aim for the large metal doors barring my exit, and without raising hands to operate the opening mechanism, I force my way through them with all of the strength in my body that the Judges allow. My wrath for being imprisoned thus is fuelled by my Ka, my essence, and the doors fly free off of their hinges as my desiccated body barrels through. I am forced to stop momentarily as my shrunken eyes blink in the harsh light of the room I\u2019ve now entered. The taste of frankincense.<br /> <br /> People stand around me, some awed, but most in abject fear, the Sybaris instilling in them such terror that they either trip over themselves in attempt to flee or collapse to the floor in a whimpering heap. All around me are metal surfaces, men and women in white, with aprons and hats. Some with knives, others with food preparation implements. I will not be threatened with a knife or spatula, and bellow a dictate for all to kneel, and answer me the question of where I am, when I am, who I am. The words are barely articulated, so poorly constructed is my mouth, so a formless roar is instead what they hear. I almost surprise myself as the noise cuts through the worktops like a demolishing hammer, knocking all aside and clearing a path for me to enter another chamber, this one housing men and women in suits. My vessels, my relics, my ornaments, all are here. All are arranged as I would expect. The amulet on the pedestal nearest to the north-east wall. The statue wreathed in bushels, next to flowing water. The unadorned pillar in the centre of the chamber. The smell of frankincense burning.<br /> <br /> The suited audience appears to have been waiting for me, as they all have smiles on their faces. They all have meals laid out on tables that arbitrarily seem to surround the historic features of this tomb. They all hold glasses, and one raises her glass aloft in a toast. She speaks words I cannot understand. \u201cTo the awakening of our master,\u201d she says, as they all drink.<br /> The smell, the flavour, the sight of my sacred geometry. As I stand in this eating area, having left my frozen tomb and torn a path through a kitchen of hapless workers, I am being welcomed by my cult, The Perfumed Ones. I am Sur-Ab-Olib, the Bearer of Incense. My cult has built a restaurant over my tomb. Now I must decide whether to scour the skin from my high priest\u2019s bones for such an affrontery or bless her for summoning me.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T05:24:26-08:00","id":4225,"title":"","content":"Thank you good sir, this is excellently written <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Assistant Organizer for:</b><br /> <a href=\"http://www.meetup.com/Dead-Gamers-Society/\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://i162.photobucket.com/albums/t261/jlburgos_bucket/a41e98d1-1eed-4506-a8d2-2b3bea4a43da_zps469395ad.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/311-joeb","name":"JoeB","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar311_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T05:39:15-08:00","id":4231,"title":"","content":"An absolute pleasure, and thank you for the kind compliment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-08T23:30:50-08:00","id":6661,"title":"","content":"Thanks to the good gentleman for a great and thoughtful review.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/277-cas","name":"CAS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar277_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"33"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}